+\subsection{Autonomous Algorithm Decomposition}
+The EI lane treats detector design as a decomposable search problem. Agentic decomposition splits the problem into candidate score families, modality subsets, calibration choices, sparse weights, threshold policy, and low-FPR objective tradeoffs. Evolutionary search explores those choices on train/CV rows only, then locks the selected composition. This framing matters because EI is not a black-box sensor and not an unreviewable neural monolith: the selected component IDs, weights, calibrator, threshold source, and score outputs are emitted as evidence artifacts and the source code remains reviewable.
